1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,840
this world is

2
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:21,840
hey what is going on here this world this world is being closed up

3
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:25,180
all because of my magic

4
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:35,820
we're leaving this place come on fight no we can't all go however

5
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:46,980
don't let go of sakura and mokuna what do you have up your sleeve you need to leave now

6
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:18,220
are you okay

7
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:22,560
i can't find magic

8
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:33,860
hey charan what mokuna the ring that's always in mokuna's ear take it

9
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:41,360
i learned about it in a dream it was from the other mokuna please do it

10
00:01:41,360 --> 00:02:04,960
go

11
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:16,400
oh

12
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:46,380
Oh, my God.

13
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:51,400
覚えている 日の光で

14
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:56,400
小鳥のように 目覚めた日を

15
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:01,400
未来なんて 当たり前に

16
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:07,400
来るものだと思っていた

17
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:13,400
好きな人とずっと 一緒にいたい

18
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:20,400
そんな単純な夢も 叶えられずに

19
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:28,400
僕らはここで 離れてしまうの

20
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:38,400
早く 一番大切な人のところへ

21
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:46,400
このまま 君を本当に失う

22
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:54,400
その前に 答えは特に 決まってる

23
00:03:54,400 --> 00:04:02,400
想いを 形に変えるんだ

24
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:12,400
時代だ

25
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:24,720
Where am I?

26
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,380
Anybody?

27
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,620
This is Japan.

28
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:32,880
Princess Tomoyo.

29
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,600
Is that you?

30
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:40,340
It's good to see you again, Kurokane.

31
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:46,500
And the voice I heard before?

32
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,280
Yes, that was me.

33
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:52,480
Go.

34
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:01,920
If you truly wish him to come with you, you must sacrifice something with the same magical

35
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,900
power in exchange.

36
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:09,020
When you heard that, you were moments from death, wounded beyond what my Shu curse could

37
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:09,340
heal.

38
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,120
People dream before they die.

39
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,420
Even a warrior like you.

40
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:20,740
So you entered my dream, and you told me how to bring him out.

41
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:25,580
With that spell, its caster must first become its core for it to work.

42
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:29,220
And so, the caster may not ever leave that place.

43
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,220
He must remain to hold the spell.

44
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:36,980
He had used up almost all of his magical power to allow the rest of you to escape.

45
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:44,720
He cast a spell on my left arm.

46
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,800
I assumed that by leaving it behind, I allowed him to escape.

47
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:52,420
Now, do you understand what true strength is?

48
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:53,760
Maybe.

49
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:58,640
Though in the process, I seem to have lost some of mine.

50
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:12,700
I killed a man.

51
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,620
Did you already know that, too, from your dreaming?

52
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:21,660
Did you know that this would happen because I took another's life?

53
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:25,740
I had hoped that, in the end, it wouldn't.

54
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:33,620
You called it a curse.

55
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:34,980
Is that why?

56
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:41,400
Aren't you going to ask me why I didn't tell you in the first place?

57
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:45,100
Knowledge without the ability to speak.

58
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:47,300
A pain only those who have had it know.

59
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:51,300
What good would it do me to blame you for the pain that you've endured?

60
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:53,540
Karogini.

61
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,340
It's all right.

62
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:58,660
I don't have any regrets whatsoever about losing my arm back there.

63
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:03,440
All my life, I've hungered for power.

64
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,760
So that no one would ever hurt what was dear to me again.

65
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,660
However, even power itself can bring pain.

66
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,200
And besides, there are things that power cannot protect.

67
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,240
I'm so proud of you.

68
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:31,040
You've finally learned what true strength is.

69
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,140
Thank you for waiting patiently.

70
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,840
Now, please, enter the room.

71
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,620
Kind, sir.

72
00:07:58,660 --> 00:07:59,160
What is it?

73
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:07,620
That was for earlier, Kurger Burger.

74
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,580
I'll get you for that.

75
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,740
Just wait.

76
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:35,800
Yes, I understand.

77
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,580
Now, be on your way.

78
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:47,320
Don't disappear.

79
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,880
Don't disappear, other one.

80
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:56,840
Sharon!

81
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:56,920
Sharon!

82
00:08:58,420 --> 00:08:59,560
Good morning!

83
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:00,700
Good morning!

84
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:01,820
How do you feel?

85
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,900
How do you feel?

86
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:04,560
Are you still hurting anywhere?

87
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,380
I'm fine.

88
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,740
Thanks for asking, Mokuna.

89
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:08,240
Sakura?

90
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,280
And Sakura?

91
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:13,860
What is this?

92
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:15,760
Sakura?

93
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:19,940
I took it upon myself to treat her injuries.

94
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,520
Thank you, Tomoyo.

95
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,940
But why is she up in a tree?

96
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:28,140
This tree is the oldest of its kind in all of Japan.

97
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:34,180
Its Sakura, or cherry blossoms, will help her, even if her body is without a soul.

98
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:39,180
This tree has your name, Sakura.

99
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:46,400
I see you've returned, Kurogane.

100
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:47,080
Yeah?

101
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:49,780
You should not address her so informally.

102
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:53,140
It seems you've improved a little since you were with us last.

103
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:53,740
Huh?

104
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,800
I welcome the other visitors as well.

105
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,360
May you find peace within this castle.

106
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:02,680
I know your journey must continue.

107
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:10,520
We have another guest.

108
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:19,140
Fuma, hi!

109
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,740
Well, long time no see, little one.

110
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:26,700
Although I suppose I really shouldn't assume that time is flow to the same pace for both of us.

111
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:27,600
That would be foolish.

112
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,020
So have you come to Japan to search for something, Fuma?

113
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:31,880
No.

114
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,880
I just have something to deliver.

115
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:39,700
Hey, uh, what is that?

116
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,660
It's a prosthetic arm.

117
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:45,660
I didn't have time to create skin for it, so I apologize for its appearance.

118
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:49,400
I thought you would want it as soon as it was done.

119
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:53,580
But why are you bringing this to me?

120
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,600
And how may I ask, do you even know about this?

121
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:58,780
Yuko filled me in on what had happened.

122
00:10:59,120 --> 00:10:59,980
Yuko did?

123
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:01,500
Yes, that's right.

124
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:03,420
She asked me to deliver this to you.

125
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:05,720
I came by it in another world.

126
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:09,100
One that's far more technologically advanced than this.

127
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:12,280
A country called Piffle.

128
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:22,200
What's the price?

129
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:25,380
Well, actually, Yuko already compensated me.

130
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,100
Oh, and speaking of Yuko...

131
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:33,120
I took the liberty of promising the payment that she required.

132
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:35,400
I'm afraid you were asleep at the time, Kuro.

133
00:11:35,400 --> 00:12:00,060
Bye, your eye color changed!

134
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,700
The secret was in my blue eyes.

135
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:04,800
They're what gave me my magic power.

136
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,240
Mokona, will you take this to the witch?

137
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,400
But why?

138
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,080
Don't worry about me.

139
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,720
I can still see just fine.

140
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,940
This is just the last remaining bit of my magical ability.

141
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,180
Don't do it!

142
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,620
You can't lose your magic!

143
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:25,660
You'll die!

144
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,500
No, I won't die.

145
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:30,940
The vampire blood I received will keep me alive for now.

146
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,120
It's all right, Mokona.

147
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:36,840
I wouldn't be willing to throw away my life as easily as that...

148
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,700
anymore.

149
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,600
Okay, Fai.

150
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:45,500
I'll send it to Yuko now.

151
00:12:45,500 --> 00:13:03,260
So it's arrived, then.

152
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,980
And now there's only one more to go.

153
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:14,240
Not bad at all.

154
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:17,000
I think I like you better this way.

155
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:18,320
Oh, shut up.

156
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,060
Well, we're cold.

157
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:19,320
Oh, let's go!

158
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:20,760
You're престil!

159
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:41,880
Shujiro!

160
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:42,520
Say, Shiro!

161
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,440
How long has it been, I wonder?

162
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:53,080
It's hard to know for sure, I suppose.

163
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:56,540
Who can tell if time flows the same for all of us?

164
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,060
That's almost exactly what you said, Fuma.

165
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,120
Is that because he's your big brother?

166
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:04,480
Well, it's a bit more complicated than that.

167
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:08,220
You're the same as ever, aren't you, brother?

168
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,620
Same to you.

169
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:17,300
Though looking at the two of you, I can't repeat the sentiment.

170
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:22,020
It seems to me that you've both changed, dramatically.

171
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,460
Especially you, magician.

172
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:28,120
You've lost all your magical powers, haven't you?

173
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,060
But gained a vampire's blood.

174
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:35,560
Oh, no!

175
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,940
It's Kamui's blood, isn't it?

176
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,060
And if it is, what then?

177
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,560
Where are they?

178
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:47,620
Both of them, Kamui and Tsubara.

179
00:14:47,620 --> 00:15:04,480
So, this is your older brother?

180
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,900
Yeah, and he's quite a handful.

181
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,400
Just like my sister.

182
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:09,660
Hmm?

183
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,720
And what do you mean by that?

184
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:16,240
I'm sure she was only kidding, weren't you, princess?

185
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:20,100
There are better ways of asking someone a question, don't you think?

186
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:22,140
Look who's talking.

187
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:22,940
Shut up!

188
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,340
He is right, you know.

189
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:25,120
Yes!

190
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:27,720
I don't remember asking for a second opinion!

191
00:15:29,620 --> 00:15:30,460
So sorry.

192
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:32,000
Why don't I try again?

193
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,880
If I'm not mistaken, you met the twin vampires.

194
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:38,460
I met them both while in a different world.

195
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:40,280
It was in Tokyo.

196
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:49,100
And now, are they still in Tokyo?

197
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:50,400
Not now.

198
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:51,480
They've moved on.

199
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,760
But that was after all of these guys left.

200
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:55,220
Where to?

201
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:58,500
You think they would tell me I'm your younger brother, after all?

202
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:02,120
Well, they say that hunters are supposed to be drawn to their quarry.

203
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:06,280
But no matter what methods I use, I can't seem to be able to find my prey.

204
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:10,620
Hmm.

205
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:14,260
Well, I'll be off to the next world, then.

206
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:20,560
Wait!

207
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:29,240
What have we here, another Shauron?

208
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:31,560
What happened to the feather?

209
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:33,320
I have it.

210
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:34,480
Right here.

211
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:36,700
Give it to me.

212
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,420
It was the land of Oto.

213
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:39,420
No, wait.

214
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:41,760
It was actually Idunas' country, wasn't it?

215
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,200
That's where I found it.

216
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:46,420
And naturally, I took it with me.

217
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:50,000
It has the power to turn the imaginary into reality.

218
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:53,020
And you think I'll hand it over?

219
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,240
That I'll just give it to you without a fight?

220
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:57,940
Give it back.

221
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:09,980
It appears you're prepared for the alternative, then.

222
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,280
I've been watching you for a long time.

223
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,900
I know who you are.

224
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:17,420
Watching me through the eyes of another you?

225
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:18,260
Yes.

226
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,040
You're just like your father.

227
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:25,080
But that's not surprising, I suppose.

228
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:36,140
Blood will always tell in the end, won't it?

229
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:43,000
Well, then.

230
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,420
Wait a moment!

231
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,660
I cannot allow you to fight like this.

232
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,400
You will destroy the castle.

233
00:17:49,400 --> 00:18:10,940
What is this?

234
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,580
It looks like a barrier.

235
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:16,540
An alternate dimension.

236
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:19,140
Yes, I'd say that's a barrier, all right.

237
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,400
We can be as reckless as we please here.

238
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:25,020
And our actions won't affect the space in reality.

239
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:29,560
However, any wounds we inflict will follow us back there.

240
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,620
All right.

241
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,700
Let us begin.

242
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:54,480
Where am I?

243
00:18:54,480 --> 00:19:00,660
Sakura, it's you.

244
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,620
I don't understand.

245
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:03,680
You know me?

246
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:05,540
I wouldn't say I know you exactly.

247
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,000
We met at Yuko's shop.

248
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,340
Oh, but you were asleep at that point, I guess.

249
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:12,600
Where are we?

250
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,600
Is this the inside of our shop?

251
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,100
No, that's not it.

252
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:19,000
Maybe, maybe this is a dream.

253
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:25,400
I think you're right.

254
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:28,100
We must be trapped within a dream.

255
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:52,500
We should have Kurogane and my sister watch their fight to its final conclusion.

256
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:57,340
I can tell that there's something you would like to speak with me about, Fi.

257
00:19:57,340 --> 00:20:01,900
From what I've been told, you're a dream watcher, aren't you?

258
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:04,520
So then you're able to tell the future through dreams.

259
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:08,220
But then, the first time that we encountered each other in Japan.

260
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:16,560
Hurry, he's dying.

261
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:20,680
If he dies, if he dies, then I'll...

262
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,360
It's all right.

263
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:25,120
Kurogane is not going to die.

264
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:30,760
I didn't sense it then.

265
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:32,720
The power of the dream watcher.

266
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:34,520
How do you explain that?

267
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,660
You and I have something in common.

268
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,100
I gave it to Yuko as payment as well.

269
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,580
I gave her my power.

270
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:44,440
And what were you paying for?

271
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:48,000
Was that the compensation Yuko asked for to bring us all here?

272
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:52,300
Those of us who can read the future are limited.

273
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:54,820
We can do nothing but see what lies ahead.

274
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,260
But still we hope.

275
00:20:56,560 --> 00:21:00,020
